    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Measure E is a countably additive measure, IsProbabilityMeasure means mass one. A Markov kernel is a measurable family of probability measures.",
      "State is NNReal times E times Nat times (Nat to E). For s=(b,u,k,h), s.1=b and s.2=(u,k,h). Nat.casesOn n y h prepends y to history. Vector products are scalar multiplication.",
      "Measure.tilted mu f normalizes exp(f) against mu. GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing nu sigma adds independent centered isotropic Gaussian noise of standard deviation sigma, so its covariance is sigma squared times identity.",
      "WassersteinSpace.wassersteinDistance is the actual extended-nonnegative quadratic transport distance used here; its square equals the infimum quadratic displacement cost over couplings. A finite cross displacement bound alone does not assert marginal second moments. klDiv is extended-nonnegative relative entropy.",
      "Measure.map is pushforward, bind integrates a measure-valued function, and dirac is point mass. P^n is n successive transitions, P^0 identity. Nonnegative integrals can be infinite. n in the displayed multiplication is cast to ENNReal, J in the accuracy expression is cast to Real."
    ]
